Subject: [PATCH] zink: keep buffers mappable when CPU-visible VRAM is missing or full

Zink places PIPE_USAGE_DEFAULT and DYNAMIC buffers, and persistent and
coherent buffers, in ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_VISIBLE, and zink_buffer_map
maps them directly for unsynchronized and plain write maps, without a
staging buffer. Two paths put such buffers in memory that is not
host-visible:

- When the device has no device-local, host-visible type, the screen filled
  the heap with the DEVICE_LOCAL types.
- When an allocation from the heap fails, allocate_bo() retried in
  ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL unless the buffer was coherent or dynamic.

On Venus, vkMapMemory of such memory asks the host for a mappable blob of
memory it did not allocate exportable ("vkr: mem is not exportable", then
"ctrl 0x10c, error 0x1200"). The map fails, and the application crashes:
Unigine Heaven with OpenGL took an access violation in viogpu_wgl.dll on an
RTX 5090 without resizable BAR, whose 246 MiB visible heap runs out. The
first path is a Venus guest with nvva's patch 0070 (which hides that heap).
The second is the out-of-memory fallback that 0085 makes reachable.

Fill a missing visible-VRAM heap with the HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT types, and
demote a failed visible-VRAM allocation to HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT whenever
the resource's memoryTypeBits allow it. Images that cannot use those types
still go to DEVICE_LOCAL. Devices whose visible VRAM is all of VRAM (AMD
APUs, resizable BAR) do not reach either path in normal use.

Evidence: docs/unigl.md, docs/evidence/unigl/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d unigl worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
index 106d126..c76ca67 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -1078,8 +1078,12 @@ allocate_bo(struct zink_screen *screen, const struct pipe_resource *templ,
       if (obj->bo || heap != ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_VISIBLE)
          break;
 
-      /* demote BAR allocations to a different heap on failure to avoid oom */
-      if (templ->flags & PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_MAP_COHERENT || templ->usage == PIPE_USAGE_DYNAMIC)
+      /* demote BAR allocations to a different heap on failure to avoid oom.
+       * Whatever is placed in the BAR heap may be mapped directly
+       * (zink_buffer_map maps unsynchronized and plain write maps without a
+       * staging buffer), so stay host-visible when the resource allows it.
+       */
+      if (zink_mem_type_idx_from_types(screen, ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT, reqs->memoryTypeBits) != UINT32_MAX)
           heap = ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT;
       else
           heap = ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL;
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
index 9084c91..87739f6 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3521,6 +3521,16 @@ zink_internal_create_screen(const struct pipe_screen_config *config, int64_t dev
          if (i == ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT_CACHED) {
             memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT]);
             screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT];
+         } else if (i == ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_VISIBLE) {
+            /* No CPU-visible VRAM. Buffers in this heap are mapped directly
+             * (persistent and coherent maps, unsynchronized and plain write
+             * maps), so the heap must stay host-visible: use host memory.
+             * Images that cannot live there are demoted to DEVICE_LOCAL by
+             * their memoryTypeBits.
+             */
+            memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT]);
+            screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_HOST_VISIBLE_COHERENT];
+            maybe_has_rebar = false;
          } else {
             memcpy(screen->heap_map[i], screen->heap_map[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL], screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL]);
             screen->heap_count[i] = screen->heap_count[ZINK_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL];
